id: pm-ts-starter-native-typescript-api
title: Enable native TypeScript contract checking when resolver identities are public
description: "Follow-up to the compiler API redesign in PR 154. Stock TypeScript 7.0.2 exports an unstable native API with structured diagnostics but no resolveModuleName/packageId contract. Its installed dist/api/sync/api.d.ts and dist/api/proto.d.ts expose source metadata without resolved-module identity. The checker currently returns compiler_unavailable for API-incompatible compilers; the repository build pin is unchanged. Add native checking only through compiler-provided resolved package identities, preserving the current 5.9.3/6.0.3 API behavior and without stdout parsing, compiler substitution or package metadata ancestry."
type: Feature
status: open
priority: 3
tags[4]: api,compatibility,follow-up,typescript
created_at: "2026-10-27T16:58:37.655Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-27T16:58:37.655Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Use a public native resolver identity API; clean and incompatible consumers pass direct diagnostic differential tests; retain the typed capability refusal until support exists; preserve all classic API and isolation regressions
